{"orgCode":"8120","name":"Commission on Peace Officer Standards and Training","agencyCode":"8000","agencyName":"General Government","description":"The mission of the Commission on Peace Officer Standards and Training (POST) is to continually enhance the professionalism of California law enforcement in serving its communities.\n\nRecognizing that effective law enforcement is the cornerstone of a free and safe society, POST is committed to a vision of the future that ensures quality, integrity, accountability, and cooperation; encourages new ideas; explores and uses appropriate technologies; and delivers relevant, client-based programs and services.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":44423,"cy":56553,"by":52030},"positions":{"py":218.3,"cy":257.2,"by":257.2},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":1959,"by":1959},"nongovernmental":{"py":34829,"cy":44339,"by":42135}}},"programs":{"id":"exp/8000/8120","kind":"department","name":"Commission on Peace Officer Standards and Training","code":"8120","amounts":{"py":44423,"cy":56553,"by":52030},"positions":{"py":218.3,"cy":257.2,"by":257.2},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":44423,"cy":56553,"by":52030}},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6500","kind":"program","name":"Standards","code":"6500","amounts":{"py":9116,"cy":14680,"by":12311},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":9116,"cy":14680,"by":12311}},"positions":{"py":105.2,"cy":122.5,"by":122.5},"description":"6500 - STANDARDS\n\nThe Standards Program establishes job-related selection and training standards for peace officers and dispatchers. It also provides management consultation to local law enforcement agencies. Activities include development of examinations and counseling local law enforcement agencies on ways to improve management practices. The Standards Program conducts applied research in the areas of peace officer selection and training, operational procedures, and program evaluation to meet statutory requirements and to provide management guidance to local law enforcement agencies. It facilitates the development and implementation of new programs for local agencies by serving as a clearinghouse of successful program information. The Standards Program also conducts peace officer feasibility studies.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":11682,"cy":18000,"by":15418}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6500/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":9116,"cy":14680,"by":12311},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":9116,"cy":14680,"by":12311}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":9116,"cy":14680,"by":12311}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6500/f0903","kind":"fund","name":"State Penalty Fund","code":"0903","amounts":{"py":2566,"cy":3320,"by":3107},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":2566,"cy":3320,"by":3107}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":2566,"cy":3320,"by":3107}}}}],"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":2566,"cy":3320,"by":3107}}},{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6505","kind":"program","name":"Training","code":"6505","amounts":{"py":8496,"cy":8477,"by":8476},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":8496,"cy":8477,"by":8476}},"positions":{"py":41.8,"cy":44.3,"by":44.3},"description":"6505 - TRAINING The Training Program increases the competency of law enforcement personnel by developing and certifying courses that meet identified training needs. This activity requires scheduling and quality control of such courses and assisting law enforcement agencies in presenting necessary training and career development programs to their officers. The Commission assesses training on a continuing basis to make sure evolving training needs are met. The curricula cover a wide variety of topics necessary to satisfy statutory and regulatory mandates, maintain competence in police work, and address the training needs of law enforcement agency personnel. Curricula content is updated regularly. The Training Program also presents advanced training for law enforcement supervisors and executives through its Command College and the Supervisory Leadership Institute, and for trainers through the Instructor Development Institute. Other specialty programs include the Institute of Criminal Investigation. Job-related selection and training standards for peace officers and dispatchers, established by the Standards Program, are enforced through inspections of local agencies receiving state aid to confirm they are adhering to minimum state standards.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":21803,"cy":29809,"by":28037}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6505/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":8496,"cy":8477,"by":8476},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":8496,"cy":8477,"by":8476}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":8496,"cy":8477,"by":8476}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6505/f0903","kind":"fund","name":"State Penalty Fund","code":"0903","amounts":{"py":13307,"cy":19373,"by":17602},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":13307,"cy":19373,"by":17602}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":13307,"cy":19373,"by":17602}}}},{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6505/f0995","kind":"fund","name":"Reimbursements","code":"0995","amounts":{"py":0,"cy":1959,"by":1959},"byFundType":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":1959,"by":1959}},"extra":{"fundType":"reimbursement","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":0,"cy":1959,"by":1959}}}}],"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":1959,"by":1959},"nongovernmental":{"py":13307,"cy":19373,"by":17602}}},{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6510","kind":"program","name":"Peace Officer Training","code":"6510","amounts":{"py":13975,"cy":20000,"by":20000},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":13975,"cy":20000,"by":20000}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"6510 - PEACE OFFICER TRAINING\n\nThe Peace Officer Training Program provides financial assistance to participating jurisdictions for instructional costs associated with selected training courses. Funding is also provided for the cost of student travel and per diem expenses associated with training presentations to enable line officers to receive in-service training in areas of critical need. To encourage and assist local law enforcement agencies to meet and maintain minimum standards in the selection and training of law enforcement officers, the Commission provides financial assistance to all 58 counties, approximately 346 cities, and numerous specialized districts and local agencies that have agreed to meet the Commission's standards.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":26941,"cy":33428,"by":33428}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6510/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":13975,"cy":20000,"by":20000},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":13975,"cy":20000,"by":20000}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":13975,"cy":20000,"by":20000}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6510/f0903","kind":"fund","name":"State Penalty Fund","code":"0903","amounts":{"py":12966,"cy":13428,"by":13428},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":12966,"cy":13428,"by":13428}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":12966,"cy":13428,"by":13428}}}}],"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":12966,"cy":13428,"by":13428}}},{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6515","kind":"program","name":"POST Administration","code":"6515","amounts":{"py":12836,"cy":13396,"by":11243},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":12836,"cy":13396,"by":11243}},"positions":{"py":71.3,"cy":90.4,"by":90.4},"description":"6515 - POST ADMINISTRATION\n\nThe objective of the Commission on Peace Officer Standards and Training is to be the leading organization in establishing professional standards, assuring top-quality training, and providing effective services to develop and support California law enforcement personnel. POST consists of multiple bureaus to ensure uniform standards and compliance are applied to over 600 law enforcement agencies and 41 basic training academies statewide.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":18826,"cy":21614,"by":19241}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6515/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":12836,"cy":13396,"by":11243},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":12836,"cy":13396,"by":11243}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":12836,"cy":13396,"by":11243}}}}],"excludedChildren":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/6515/f0903","kind":"fund","name":"State Penalty Fund","code":"0903","amounts":{"py":5990,"cy":8218,"by":7998},"byFundType":{"nongovernmental":{"py":5990,"cy":8218,"by":7998}},"extra":{"fundType":"nongovernmental","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":5990,"cy":8218,"by":7998}}}}],"excluded":{"nongovernmental":{"py":5990,"cy":8218,"by":7998}}}],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/8120","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/8120"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/8000/8120.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"PROGRAM AUTHORITY\n\n6500-Standards:\nPenal Code sections 13503, 13512, 13513, and 13551.\n\n6505-Training:\nPenal Code sections 13503 and 13508.\n\n6510-Peace Officer Training:\nPenal Code sections 13500 to 13526.3 and Health and Safety Code section 11489."},"excluded":{"reimbursement":{"py":0,"cy":1959,"by":1959},"nongovernmental":{"py":34829,"cy":44339,"by":42135}}},"funding":{"id":"exp/8000/8120/funding","kind":"root","name":"Commission on Peace Officer Standards and Training: Funding by fund and appropriation","amounts":{"py":44423,"cy":56553,"by":52030},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":44423,"cy":56553,"by":52030}},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/8120/fundin